        "title": "Cognitive Science Applied: Spacing and Retrieval",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "Cognitive science has produced the most robust, well-replicated, and practically actionable findings in education research. Three phenomena in particular -- spacing, retrieval practice, and interleaving -- have large effect sizes, replicate across settings, and are systematically underused in actual educational practice. The central irony: learners prefer strategies that feel productive but don't work well; the strategies that work feel harder and less comfortable."
